<!-- Anatomic-pathology cases for the prior results panel. Patient 1 owns
    orders 101 to 114, patient 2 owns order 201, and order 301 has no sample_human
    row at all. An order has at most one sample_human row (the schema keeps samp_id
    unique). Order 111 holds a plain program_sample, a program that is not anatomic
    pathology. Case ids are distinct across the four case tables, and every child
    row carries last_updated, the row's optimistic-lock version. The dataset
    leaves out dictionary, type_of_sample, localization and sample_item on purpose:
    a table named in a dataset is emptied, and through localization so are test,
    test_section and panel, for every later test class in the Surefire fork.
    The dictionary entries 9001 (Adenocarcinoma, active), 9002 (Old term, inactive)
    and 9003 (HSIL, active) and the sample items are inserted by the test setup
    and removed after it. Stored conclusions: case 11 holds the codes 9001 and
    9002 in that row order, then a text; case 17 holds a code with no dictionary
    entry (99999) and a text; case 14 holds a blank text only. Patient 3 owns
    orders 401 to 405, so the lists of patients 1 and 2 are unchanged: case 23
    is on screen and its earlier cytology cases are 35 (unsatisfactory, negative
    flag left at its default), 36 (unsatisfactory, no diagnosis row), 37 (no
    diagnosis row, no adequacy) and 38 (satisfactory, negative). -->

